OmegaY/ and OmegaY.lean are adapted from the first project.  Each file starts
with a header naming its original path and revision and stating what was
changed.  The changes in the code are:
  * the lemma `YesMetaZFC.BMS.transGen_head` is replaced by
    `Por.BMS.transGen_head` of this repository (same statement), in three files;
  * the semantic layer is replaced.  OmegaY/Reflection/Interface.lean keeps the
    interface definitions of OmegaY/Reflection.lean unchanged.
    OmegaY/Reflection.lean and OmegaY/Reflection/OrdinalSupply.lean keep the
    statements the core calls (`R`, `key_weaken`, `finite_reflection`, `Label`,
    `top`, `initial_finite_graph`) and prove them from the model in Por/;
    OmegaY/Reflection/Skolem.lean and OmegaY/Reflection/Stability.lean are not
    included;
  * OmegaY/KeyReflection.lean imports OmegaY.Reflection instead of
    OmegaY.Reflection.Stability, and OmegaY/Audit.lean also audits `Por`.

Por/Formula.lean, Por/Relation.lean and Por/Supply.lean (the
patterns-of-resemblance model) are written for this repository.  Por/Supply.lean
adapts `Label`, `top`, `countable_iio_ordinal` and `countable_iio` from
OmegaY/Reflection/OrdinalSupply.lean of the first project, and says so in its
header.

ZeroY/ (20 modules) is taken from koteitan/1y-wo-por
(https://github.com/koteitan/1y-wo-por, Apache-2.0), which adapted it from
`formalization/ZeroY` of the second project; each file keeps its header.  The
imports and namespaces of the BMS layer are renamed to `Por.BMS`, and
`ZeroY/BMS/AnyArray.lean` is not included.

Por/BMS/ is taken from koteitan/1y-wo-por, where it was written for that
repository by the same author.  No code from the snapshot of YesMetaZFC /
BMS-Well-Ordering-Lean that the first project depends on, which carries no
license, is copied or adapted here.
